  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="745e-76c3-7ded-7edb" name="Trojan War (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #120 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This list covers the most famous of ancient conflicts, and the later armies of the Mycenean culture until it was overrun by invaders from the north. Both sides in the war fought in the same way. Ideally armies should be a grouping of several heroes and their retinues. It seems that the earlier method of fighting had not completely died out, so you can model old Nestor’s contingent, for example, by using the troop types from the earlier list. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Trojan War]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry: up to 50% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
